  "body": "## What changed\n\nAdd `cargo xtask merge-plan --check` for premerge validation of wave 1.\n\n- Check the simulated merged commit in a temporary detached worktree.\n- Run `cargo check --tests` for the touched workspace packages, one package at a time.\n- Attribute compiler errors to PRs through their changed files.\n- Exclude those PRs and their stacked children. Replan and check the remaining wave.\n- Exclude the whole wave when a compiler error has no identified owner.\n- Report exclusions in text and JSON. Return exit 1 for exclusions and exit 2 for operational errors.\n- Remove the trial worktree on success and failure. Preserve the caller's branch and files.\n- Require this step in the merge-ready skill before the first merge.\n\nThe default planner still checks text conflicts without a build. The trial check reuses `target/` and does not link test binaries.\n\n## Why\n\nTwo heads can compile separately and merge without a text conflict, but fail together.\nThe regression adds a struct field on one branch and a test initializer on the other.\nThe merged check finds E0063 for the missing `sharp_corners` field before any real merge.\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/3459-merge-trial.md`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cargo test -p xtask --test merge_review --test merge_ready_skill -- --nocapture`: PASS.\n  - `trial::text_clean_missing_field_is_excluded_before_real_merge`.\n  - `trial::individual_heads_compile_and_leave_no_trial_worktree`.\n  - `trial::a_stacked_child_of_an_excluded_owner_is_not_proposed`.\n  - `trial::metadata_failure_cleans_the_trial_and_does_not_emit_a_plan`.\n  - `merge_ready_checks_the_merged_wave_before_the_first_merge`.\n- The regression fails with trial validation disabled. It passes with validation enabled.\n- `cargo test -p xtask --bin xtask merge_trial::`: PASS, including package selection and diagnostic ownership.\n- `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=3 cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: PASS on the final source tree.\n- `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings`: blocked by the unchanged `clippy::needless_bool` in `xtask/src/unit_sweep.rs:67`.\n- The same clippy command with only `-A clippy::needless_bool`: PASS.\n- Focused rustfmt checks and `git diff --check`: PASS.\n\n## Limits\n\nThe check proves compilation, not runtime behavior. It does not replace independent review.\nNo geometry, toolpath, post, application, or workflow code changed.\nThe light plan was inspected, not executed. It contains only motion and app release steps; none checks this tooling change.\nNo full workspace, application, GUI, catalog-program, heavy, or release certification is claimed.\nNo maintainer runner was used. No merge or auto-merge is requested.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: medium\nProcess change: yes\n\nFixes #3459\n",
